    "# Bare-Metal Profiling - Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "What the hybrid simulator cannot do when you profile a **bare-metal** program:\n",
    "one standalone application, single privilege (M-mode), **no OS / no Linux\n",
    "kernel**, and **no co-simulation**.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a focused subset of `andes_sim_limitations.ipynb`. That master doc\n",
    "lists every limitation and owns the `L`-ids; this notebook keeps only the ones\n",
    "a bare-metal user actually hits, written as a short \"do / do not\" tutorial.\n",
    "For anything outside this use case (OS / Linux workloads, S-mode paging,\n",
    "lock-step co-sim) read the master doc.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two kinds of entry below:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Hard limit** - the run hangs, crashes, or returns a wrong result.\n",
    "- **Accuracy caveat** - the run finishes, but the cycle number can mislead.\n",
    "\n",
    "Every claim is backed by a cell that runs a real command against this repo."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "Already built: the driver (`build/andes-sim`), the vsim engine, and the test\n",
    "fixtures (`tests/fixtures/*.elf`). The `break_*` fixtures misbehave on purpose\n",
    "and are built individually. If anything is missing, run `source ./setup.sh`\n",
    "from the repo root."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "cell-2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
