  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The one rule: keep the measured window simple\n",
    "\n",
    "Profiling measures one region of your program - the **ROI**, between the entry\n",
    "and exit triggers. When the run hands that region to the cycle-accurate vsim\n",
    "engine, only part of the CPU state crosses the boundary. So the measured region\n",
    "MUST stay inside this envelope:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **One privilege level** throughout (bare metal = M-mode). No privilege change\n",
    "  inside the ROI.\n",
    "- **No paging** (`satp = 0`). Bare metal already runs in bare address mode, so\n",
    "  this is free - just do not turn paging on.\n",
    "- **No held atomic** (`lr`/`sc`) reservation across the entry trigger.\n",
    "- **Effectively trap-free.** A simple synchronous M-mode trap + handler is OK\n",
    "  (shown below); delegation and page faults are not.\n",
    "- **No asynchronous interrupts** inside the window.\n",
    "- **I/O only through the vplat runtime** (UART2 + SimControl). No semihosting.\n",
    "\n",
    "Step outside the envelope and the result is silently wrong or the run hangs.\n",
    "Each item below is one consequence of this rule."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## I/O: link the vplat runtime, never semihosting  (L1)\n",
    "\n",
    "A bare-metal program still needs `printf` / `exit` / file I/O. Use the **vplat\n",
    "runtime**, which routes them to MMIO devices both engines model (stdio ->\n",
    "UART2, exit -> SimControl, files -> HTIF). Link it with\n",
    "`-B build/runtime -specs=andes-sim.specs`; every C fixture in this repo does.\n",
    "\n",
    "Do NOT link a semihosting libgloss (`-lgloss_vh`). vsim has no semihosting\n",
    "handler, so the semihosting `ebreak` traps, the handler calls `_exit` (another\n",
    "`ebreak`), and the run loops forever until it times out.\n",
    "\n",
    "Below, `vplat_hello.elf` prints from INSIDE the measured window - serviced by\n",
    "the cycle-accurate vsim leg - and still yields a clean `window_cycles`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "cell-5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[andes-sim] model=hybrid engine=vsim:ax45mpv_premium vlen=512 trigger=pc fixture=vplat_hello\n",
      "[hsim mmap] 128.0 MiB at /dev/shm (free: 251.4 GiB)\n",
      "Copyright (C) 2013-2026 Andes Technology Corporation. All rights reserved.\n",
      "Version : unknown\n",
      "\n",
      "hello from vplat\n",
      "[pc window_cycles] 3400  (vsim mcycle=2189983807566868 - qemu mcycle=2189983807563468)\n",
      "PASS: --model hybrid --trigger pc (vplat_hello)"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!andes-sim run --model hybrid --trigger pc --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium \\\n",
    "    --pc-start say_hello --pc-end vplat_roi_end tests/fixtures/vplat_hello.elf"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Hard limits - the run hangs, crashes, or is wrong"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L5. An atomic (`lr`/`sc`) cannot span the entry trigger\n",
    "\n",
    "If `lr.{w,d}` runs before the trigger and the matching `sc.{w,d}` runs after\n",
    "it, the reservation - microarchitectural state, not part of the handoff - is\n",
    "lost. vsim resumes with no reservation, the `sc` always fails, and a\n",
    "compare-exchange loop spins forever.\n",
    "\n",
    "Keep any `lr`/`sc` pair and its retry loop entirely on one side of the trigger.\n",
    "`break_lrsc.elf` holds a reservation across the boundary on purpose:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "cell-8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[standalone fast] PASS: sc succeeded (reservation survived)\n",
      "[andes-sim] model=hybrid engine=vsim:ax45mpv_premium vlen=512 trigger=marker fixture=break_lrsc\n",
      "[hsim mmap] 128.0 MiB at /dev/shm (free: 251.4 GiB)\n",
      "[hybrid] exit 124 (124 = killed = the documented hang: reservation lost)"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Standalone (one engine, no handoff): reservation survives, sc succeeds.\n",
    "!andes-sim run --model fast tests/fixtures/break_lrsc.elf \\\n",
    "    && echo \"[standalone fast] PASS: sc succeeded (reservation survived)\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Hybrid: lr.d on QEMU1, sc.d on vsim with no reservation -> sc fails ->\n",
    "# the program spins. The kill (exit 124) IS the limitation.\n",
    "!timeout 30 andes-sim run --model hybrid --trigger marker \\\n",
    "    --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium tests/fixtures/break_lrsc.elf ; \\\n",
    " echo \"[hybrid] exit $? (124 = killed = the documented hang: reservation lost)\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L4. Traps: a simple M-mode trap works; delegation / page faults do not\n",
    "\n",
    "Good news for bare metal: the writable trap CSRs (`mepc`, `mcause`, `mtval`,\n",
    "`mie`, `mip`) and `mtvec` cross the handoff, so a handler installed before the\n",
    "ROI is reachable and a **synchronous M-mode trap taken inside the ROI returns\n",
    "correctly**.\n",
    "\n",
    "What is NOT supported: `medeleg` / `mideleg` are not restored (no delegation to\n",
    "S-mode), and with paging off there is no page-fault path. So the safe rule\n",
    "stays \"trap-free\", with the single exception of a plain synchronous M-mode\n",
    "trap.\n",
    "\n",
    "`rt_trap_ecall.elf` takes two `ecall`s inside the ROI, each handled by an\n",
    "`mret`; the run completes with a normal cycle count:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "cell-10",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[andes-sim] model=hybrid engine=vsim:ax45mpv_premium vlen=512 trigger=pc fixture=rt_trap_ecall\n",
      "[hsim mmap] 128.0 MiB at /dev/shm (free: 251.2 GiB)\n",
      "Copyright (C) 2013-2026 Andes Technology Corporation. All rights reserved.\n",
      "Version : unknown\n",
      "\n",
      "[pc window_cycles] 416  (vsim mcycle=2195762264880320 - qemu mcycle=2195762264879904)\n",
      "PASS: --model hybrid --trigger pc (rt_trap_ecall)"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!andes-sim run --model hybrid --trigger pc --pc-start roi_start --pc-end hang \\\n",
    "    --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium tests/fixtures/rt_trap_ecall.elf"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L9. Only the vplat devices work inside the ROI\n",
    "\n",
    "Both engines model exactly two device ranges: **UART2** (`0xf0300000`) and\n",
    "**SimControl/HTIF** (`0xe0080000`) - that is what makes vplat I/O work. Any\n",
    "other device touched inside the ROI (PLIC, the timer `mtime`/`mtimecmp`, ROM,\n",
    "custom MMIO) is engine-specific and will not behave consistently. And no device\n",
    "STATE crosses the handoff (UART FIFO, pending interrupts, timer compare) - only\n",
    "RAM is shared. Keep peripheral and timer access out of the measured window."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "cell-12",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "95:    [ANDES_AE350_SIM_CONTROL]       = { 0xe0080000,       0x1000 },\n",
      "107:    [ANDES_AE350_UART2]             = { 0xf0300000,     0x100000 },"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!grep -nE \"ANDES_AE350_(SIM_CONTROL|UART2)\\b.*0x\" QEMU/hw/riscv/andes_ae350.c"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L8. One hart only\n",
    "\n",
    "The resume/drain path, the icount counter, and BBV emit all assume a single\n",
    "hart. Multi-hart configs (`_NDS_NHART=2`), IPIs, and hart-to-hart sync are out\n",
    "of scope; resuming hart 1 from hart 0 state corrupts both."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "cell-14",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "qemu_plugin/bbv_emit.h:9:// Single-hart only - matches the broader hybrid plan-validation\n",
      "verilator/src/hybrid/icount_trigger.hpp:14:// Multi-hart out of scope - the counter is a single uint64_t, sized for one"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!grep -niE \"single-hart only|multi-hart out of scope\" \\\n",
    "    qemu_plugin/bbv_emit.h verilator/src/hybrid/icount_trigger.hpp"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-15",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L3. Paging stays off (`satp` is not restored)\n",
    "\n",
    "`satp` is carried in the state file but never written back into vsim, so the\n",
    "ROI always runs in bare address mode. For bare metal that is exactly what you\n",
    "want - just do not enable paging inside the measured region, or every virtual\n",
    "address would be treated as physical and hit the wrong memory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "cell-16",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "55:  static constexpr uint16_t kCsrSatp     = 0x180;\n",
      "224:    // mirrors as a no-op. medeleg/mideleg/satp stay unrestored -- they are"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!grep -ni \"satp\" verilator/src/hybrid/resume_driver.hpp"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-17",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L7. Watch the RAM ceiling\n",
    "\n",
    "Default guest RAM is 128 MiB; `--mem-size` raises it up to a hard 2 GiB - 4 KiB\n",
    "(the AE350 DRAM window). The STATIC image is checked at load time - an ELF whose\n",
    "segments overrun `--mem-size` is rejected with a clear message. But RUNTIME\n",
    "growth is NOT checked: if the heap or stack grows past the ceiling, the access\n",
    "is silently dropped or mis-routed and nothing names `--mem-size` as the cause.\n",
    "Size `--mem-size` for your peak heap + stack."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "cell-18",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "353:  long long mem = 128LL * 1024 * 1024;  // shared mmap; --mem-size overrides\n",
      "358:    // Early cap: QEMU's AE350 DRAM window is 2 GiB and the backend doubles as\n",
      "360:    // program's RAM (L26/F2), so the usable --mem-size is 2 GiB minus that"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!grep -nE \"128LL|GiB|usable --mem-size\" driver/cmd_run.cpp | head -5"
   ]
  },
