   "id": "cell-19",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Accuracy caveats - the run finishes, but the number can mislead"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-20",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L25. Do not read or write time-variant CSRs in the ROI\n",
    "\n",
    "Treat `mcycle` (0xB00), `minstret` (0xB02), `mip` (0x344), and `time` (0xC01)\n",
    "as opaque inside the ROI - no branch, arithmetic, or write on them. QEMU\n",
    "approximates counts (CPI~=1); vsim counts real pipeline cycles, so these values\n",
    "diverge at every point in the window by construction.\n",
    "\n",
    "Writing `mcycle` is the clearest trap: `csrw mcycle, zero` makes the drain\n",
    "re-read a reset value, so the reported `window_cycles` underflows into garbage\n",
    "- while the run still reports PASS. `break_mcycle_write.elf` does exactly this:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "cell-21",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[marker window_cycles] 18444548411405810919  (vsim mcycle=20215 - qemu mcycle=2195662303760912)\n",
      "PASS: --model hybrid --trigger marker (break_mcycle_write)"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!andes-sim run --model hybrid --trigger marker \\\n",
    "    --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium tests/fixtures/break_mcycle_write.elf \\\n",
    "    2>&1 | grep -E \"window_cycles|PASS|FAIL\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-22",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L2. PMP protection is not carried into the ROI (M-mode)\n",
    "\n",
    "The producer's PMP config is drained but, for an M-mode handoff, never written\n",
    "back into vsim - so the ROI runs with zeroed PMP. Because M-mode bypasses\n",
    "unlocked entries, the usual symptom is the opposite of a fault: an access the\n",
    "producer locked down just succeeds. If your bare-metal code relies on\n",
    "PMP-enforced regions inside the ROI, that protection silently disappears. The\n",
    "mirror is gated on `state.priv != 3` (only S/U handoffs get it):"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "cell-23",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "177:    if (state.priv != 3) {"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!grep -n \"state.priv != 3\" verilator/src/hybrid/resume_driver.hpp"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-24",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L21. Most Andes vendor CSRs are not carried\n",
    "\n",
    "Only the cache/misc pair `mcache_ctl` (0x7CA) and `mmisc_ctl` (0x7D0) crosses\n",
    "the handoff - they matter because crt0 enables the L1 caches there, and without\n",
    "them the whole window would run uncached and inflate the cycle count\n",
    "severalfold. Every OTHER Andes vendor CSR (`mmsc_cfg`, `micm_cfg`, `mdcm_cfg`,\n",
    "`mxstatus`, ...) keeps its vsim reset value, so any prefetcher / branch-\n",
    "predictor / ECC control your program tuned is ignored in the measurement - an\n",
    "accuracy hazard."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "cell-25",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "60:  static constexpr uint16_t kCsrMcacheCtl = 0x7CA;\n",
      "61:  static constexpr uint16_t kCsrMmiscCtl  = 0x7D0;\n",
      "240:    write_csr_tolerant(kCsrMcacheCtl, state.mcache_ctl);\n",
      "241:    write_csr_tolerant(kCsrMmiscCtl,  state.mmisc_ctl);"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!grep -n \"kCsrMcacheCtl\\|kCsrMmiscCtl\" verilator/src/hybrid/resume_driver.hpp"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-26",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### L14. SimPoint cycle estimate is an approximation\n",
    "\n",
    "If you use `--mode simpoint` to estimate whole-program cycles, the headline\n",
    "number is `N_total * weighted_CPI` sampled from one window per phase, with no\n",
    "error bound. Each window starts cold (caches, predictor) unless you pass\n",
    "`--vsim-warmup-icount`, which biases CPI high without it. Read the estimate as\n",
    "approximate, and always warm up."
   ]
  },
